 text←ToChar mixed;dr
⍝ Convert characters and/or numeric Unicode code-points into Dyalog Unicode-text

 :If ##.IsChar text←1/mixed ⍝ The usual case
     ⍝ We should be able to use this as-is
 :ElseIf ##.IsInt text
     'DOMAIN ERROR: Unicode values out of range'##.Error∨/~(0∘≤∧≤∘65535)text
     text←⎕UCS⌊0.5+text ⍝ Convert this whole thing to text first
 :ElseIf ∧/0 1 2 3 5∊⍨dr←10|⎕DR¨text ⍝ Check if it's mixed text and numbers
     'DOMAIN ERROR: Unicode values out of range'##.Error∨/~(0∘≤∧≤∘65535)(dr∊1 3 5)/text
     text←{⎕UCS⌊0.5+⍵}@(⍸dr∊1 3 5)⊢text ⍝ Convert only the numbers to text
 :Else
     ##.Error'∆WI DOMAIN ERROR: Text' ⍝? Is this the right message when used with '?Text'? Or do I need to use ChangeError?
 :EndIf
